{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #217: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. For which $n$ are there $n$ points in $\\mathbb{R}^2$, no three on a line and no four on a circle, which determine $n-1$ distinct distances and so that (in some ordering of the distances) the $i$th distance occurs $i$ times? Current best: Erd\\H{o}s originally believed this was impossible for $n\\geq 5$, but Pomerance constructed a set with $n=5$ (see \\cite{Er83c} for a description), and Pal\\'{a}sti has proved such sets exist for all $n\\leq 8$. Prize: no. Tags: distances, geometry."},"claim_id":"vcl_a76e398991b328d9b2543802a133a7647a88e322211fab5f4773fb0f38bd82bb","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:217","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_6c79f9c2156124eb","object_root":"sha256:d3918db8d19bdefca279dbb0d5499e50d939b65061e7195aee7a1a46ee6a831f","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:217"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"v